  {ico: "network", title: "DNS management", text: "The records that point your domain at your website and mail, kept correct as things change."},
  {ico: "wrench", title: "Mail migration", text: "Moving from another provider? We plan the move, copy existing mail across and agree the timing with you first."},
  {ico: "shield", title: "Spam filtering", text: "Server-side filtering that stops the obvious junk before it reaches you, with a Junk folder you can check and correct."},
  {ico: "eye", title: "Delivery problems", text: "Mail landing in someone&rsquo;s junk folder, or not arriving at all? We&rsquo;ll find out why and explain it in plain language."}
])
$e2 = tiles("grid3", [
  {ico: "lock", title: "SPF", text: "A public list of the servers allowed to send mail for your domain. Receivers check it to spot mail sent from somewhere it shouldn&rsquo;t be."},
  {ico: "shield", title: "DKIM", text: "A signature added to every message you send. It lets the receiver confirm the mail really came from your domain and was not altered on the way."},
  {ico: "eye", title: "DMARC", text: "Your instruction to receivers on what to do with mail that fails those checks, and a way to get reports on who is sending as you."}
])
$le1 = lede("What we look after", "Email that works, at your own address.", "Email is the part of being online that people notice first when it goes wrong. We set it up properly and stay on the other end of the phone.")
$le2 = lede("Authentication, explained", "Three records that decide whether your mail is trusted.", "Large mail providers increasingly expect all three. Getting them right is one of the most effective things you can do for delivery, and we set them up as part of the job.")
